    "message": {
     "content": "### 1. The Financial Breakdown: A Massive Shift\n\nThe addition of the **\\$200,000 sign-on bonus** fundamentally transforms this offer. It fully replaces the \\$200,000 in unvested Meta RSUs in **liquid cash** while keeping your base pay whole and delivering an increase in target bonus percentage (20% vs. ~15%).\n\n#### 4-Year Total Compensation Comparison\n\n| Component | Meta (Annual / 4-Yr Projected) | Google Revised (4-Yr Total) | Google Annualized Avg |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | \\$240,000 / \\$960,000 | \\$240,000 / \\$960,000 | \\$240,000 |\n| **Bonus** | \\$36,000 / \\$144,000 | \\$48,000 / \\$192,000 | \\$48,000 |\n| **Equity (4-Yr)** | ~\\$1,000,000 | \\$1,080,000 | \\$270,000 |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | \\$0 | \\$200,000 | \\$50,000 |\n| **Total 4-Yr Comp** | **~\\$2,104,000** | **\\$2,432,000** | **~\\$608,000/yr** |\n\n*(Note: These figures exclude equity refreshers and stock appreciation at both companies.)*\n\n---\n\n### 2. What Year 1 Looks Like\n\nDepending on whether Google grants this on their standard front-loaded schedule (33% / 33% / 22% / 12%) or a standard 25% linear schedule, your **Year 1 cash + equity payout** will be:\n\n* **If Front-Loaded (33% Y1):**\n  * \\$240k Base + \\$48k Bonus + \\$356.4k Equity + \\$200k Sign-on = **~\\$844,400 in Year 1**\n* **If Linear (25% Y1):**\n  * \\$240k Base + \\$48k Bonus + \\$270.0k Equity + \\$200k Sign-on = **~\\$758,000 in Year 1**\n\nIn either case, you are taking home **\\$230,000 to \\$318,000 more in Year 1** than staying at Meta.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Should You Take It?\n\n**Yes, you should strongly consider accepting**, provided the team and product domain appeal to you.\n\nBecause the recruiter matched your base and handed you \\$200k in guaranteed sign-on cash, the financial friction and transition risk of leaving Meta have been fully compensated.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Final Due Diligence Before Signing\n\nBefore you sign the final paperwork, verify these three operational details with the recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-on Payment Timing & Clawback:**\n   * Confirm whether the \\$200,000 is paid out as a **single lump sum in your first 30 days** or split between Year 1 and Year 2.\n   * Standard Google clawback is 12 months (pro-rated). Ensure it is not a 24-month clawback.\n2. **Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Confirm whether the grant follows the 33/33/22/12 schedule or 25% equal quarterly vesting so you can model your personal tax withholding and Year 3 cash flow.\n3. **Team & Scope Placement:**\n   * Since you are an established IC6 at Meta, ensure you have direct alignment with your prospective Google Director/VP on product scope, headcount ownership, and clear ownership boundaries. Meta PMs often find Google\u2019s consensus-driven culture a shift from Meta's faster-moving execution model; having clear scope from Day 1 is critical.",
